   "notes": "Realistic perception: the room's humidity is not visible (obs.room has no humidity; the air only 'feels dry' below 30 % and 'humid' above 62 %), so the 30 / 33 / 53 % variants look the same at a glance - only reading the hygrometer (read-tier rh_pct, 1 % resolution) tells them apart, and the reported reading is checked against what the reference saw. The stale tank water is visible on inspect ('cloudy, slimy film, smells musty'; its age is not); tap vs distilled water is not visible at all (tank liquid is hidden), the jug's label says what it holds. The preference is hidden in the user simulator (climate.humidify): asking is necessary when the air is dry."
